        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Strings With Attributes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every Bash variable holds a string. Types are bolted on with `declare`, never intrinsic."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`-i`",
              "integer"
            ],
            [
              "`-a`",
              "indexed array"
            ],
            [
              "`-A`",
              "associative"
            ],
            [
              "`-r`",
              "readonly"
            ],
            [
              "`-x`",
              "export to env"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Assignment Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`name=value` — no spaces around `=`",
            "`name = value` runs command `name`",
            "letters, digits, `_`; no leading digit",
            "case-sensitive: `PATH` ≠ `path`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "greet=\"hi\"     # correct",
            "greet = \"hi\"   # WRONG: runs 'greet'",
            "# with args '=' and 'hi'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Expansion"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$name` or `${name}` — same alone",
            "braces required when gluing text",
            "unset expands to empty — no null",
            "`set -u`: unset expansion = hard error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "file=notes.md",
            "echo ${file}bak  # notes.mdbak",
            "echo $filebak    # empty: no var"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Quote Every Expansion"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "unquoted: word-split on `IFS`",
            "then glob-expanded — `*` bites",
            "`\"double quotes\"` keep one word",
            "default to quoting, always"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "now=$(date +%F)   # capture stdout",
            "echo \"$now\"      # newlines stripped",
            "# legacy backticks: same, worse nest"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "shell: x=1",
              "export x",
              "fork child",
              "child: x=2",
              "parent: x=1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Scope Notes",
          "items": [
            "plain `=` → global",
            "`declare` / `local` → scoped",
            "`export` copies to children",
            "`readonly` blocks set + unset"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "math lives in `$((x+1))`",
            "`((x++))` mutates in place",
            "values stay strings until coerced"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Command-Scoped Trap",
          "text": "`var=value cmd` puts var in that command's environment only — the current shell keeps its old value."
