          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Quote, Don't Join",
          "text": "Unquoted `$@` and `$*` are identical — both word-split and globbed. The classic bug is missing quotes, not the wrong symbol."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Family, No Forks",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The `${name...}` operators run at expansion time, inside the shell — zero subprocesses."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Op",
            "Fires when",
            "Action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`${v:-w}`",
              "unset or empty",
              "use w"
            ],
            [
              "`${v-w}`",
              "unset only",
              "use w"
            ],
            [
              "`${v:=w}`",
              "unset or empty",
              "assign w"
            ],
            [
              "`${v:+w}`",
              "set + non-empty",
              "use w"
            ],
            [
              "`${v:?m}`",
              "unset or empty",
              "die with m"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Memory Hook",
          "text": "No colon = unset only; colon = unset or empty. Trailing symbol picks the action: `-` use, `=` assign, `+` replace, `?` die."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mutates Or Not"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "${v:-w}",
                "lines": [
                  "read-only default",
                  "var untouched after"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "${v:=w}",
                "lines": [
